HST Office: picture, frame and object dialogs with Word's Layout tabs. Position, Text Wrapping and Size are
tabs at one level, followed by the alt text and the other pages. Text Wrapping offers Word's seven styles.

- SwFramePage keeps owning the position and size widgets, because each limits the other. In the frame dialogs
  the Size tab shows hstFrameSize, moved there with weld::Container::move, and forwards page changes to the
  position page. The frame style dialog has no such tab and keeps both on one page.
- The seven styles are a view on what the page already stores. Tight is contour and outside, Through is contour,
  Behind and In Front are wrap through with or without background, In Line sets the anchor as character. Word's
  sides are the old Parallel, Before, After and Optimal; contour, background, first paragraph and overlap stay
  under Advanced.
- Page ids type, wrap, options, picture, crop, borders, area, transparence, hyperlink, macro are unchanged.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); hstframesizepage.ui is new, MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-writer.py picture frame
